      <activity id="950edcca-7a8e-5ffd-8b40-1dc2240b3ac8" activityNameId="1c5dd460-edc0-5218-adad-8db67e07e891" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, at cogen 1MWth, wood chips, economic allocation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, at cogen 1MWth, wood chips, economic allocation
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from wood chips, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 1MWth. The multioutput process "wood chips, burned in cogen 1MWth" delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 1MWth, wood chips, economic allocation" and "electricity, at cogen 1MWth, wood chips, economic allocation". The energy efficiency is 35% for electricity and 45% for heat. The economic factor is 0.77 for electricity and 0.23 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.72 for electricity and 0.28 for heat.
Included are the wood chips burning in a 1MWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and economic allocation is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland. 
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_38630142-ef62-39b3-98da-65a78d42749d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
